# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project 7 — what does and does not belong in version control.
#
# Ava needs to open the normalised data and the results without rebuilding
# anything, so the canonical cohort and every results table ARE tracked.
# What stays out is material that is either
#   (a) not ours to redistribute — journal PDFs and publisher supplementary,
#   (b) unreadable to a human and regenerable — R .rds caches, or
#   (c) a large public download that a script re-fetches — GEO, GENCODE, DICE.
#
# Rule of thumb: if you would open it to check a number, it is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# === TRACKED — listed so nobody re-excludes them by accident ===============
#   data/cohort_474/**      canonical cohort: counts, metadata, sample list
#   **/results/**           every results table from every arm
#   cibersortx/data/*.csv   QC screen and gene-mapping reports

# === (a) copyrighted third-party material ==================================
# Cite these; don't redistribute them. Download your own via the library.
**/paper/
**/data/supplementary/
**/data/reference/
*.pdf
**/docs/*fulltext*.txt
**/docs/supplementary_methods.txt
**/docs/supplementary_figures*.txt

# === (b) binary caches — unreadable and regenerable ========================
*.rds
**/bmind_chunks/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# === (c) large public downloads a script re-fetches ========================
# Recover all of these with the download_data.sh scripts. Checksums stay
# tracked, so a fresh clone can verify it got byte-identical data.
**/data/raw/
**/data/external/
**/data/raw_as_deposited/*.gz
*.gtf.gz

# Paper-reproduction intermediates: these exist only to rebuild the two
# published analyses, and data/cohort_474/ is canonical for our own work,
# so tracking them would add ~150 MB of duplicates. Rebuild with
# 00_prepare_data.py in each folder.
Krebs Paper/data/processed/
Boltz Paper/data/processed/

# Superseded CIBERSORTx inputs — cohort_474 carries the canonical mixture.
# Regenerate with `python cibersortx/subset_mixture.py`.
cibersortx/data/mixture_TPM_hgnc_480.txt
cibersortx/data/mixture_TPM_hgnc_analysis_431.txt

# The full CIBERSORTx upload matrix is 102 MB, which GitHub rejects outright
# (hard limit 100 MB per file). It is exactly reproducible:
#     python data/make_mixture_full.py
# from counts_474.tsv.gz, which IS tracked, and mixture_full_474.sha256 (also
# tracked) verifies the rebuild byte for byte.
data/cohort_474/mixture_TPM_hgnc_full_474.txt

# === keep these despite the rules above ====================================
!**/CHECKSUMS.sha256
!**/data/**/README.md
!**/data/**/*.py
!**/data/**/*.R

# === editor / OS cruft =====================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.venv/
venv/

# Network arm scratch cache (rebuilt by network/00_load.R in ~40 s)
network/cache/
